  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Voluntary Relocation from Italy to Other EU Member and Associated States - RELITA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is intended to contribute towards enhanced solidarity among EU Member States (EUMS) and associated states through relocation of applicants of international protection from Italy to other EUMS and associated countries. The project seeks to ensure the safe transfer of up to 2,200 people over 12 months, starting from 1 September 2020, this way ensuring continuity in the efforts already undertaken by the Italian Government. IOM, in close cooperation with national counterparts, countries of relocation and the EU, takes care of pre-departure activities, specifically looking at pre-migration health assessment and pre-departure embarkation checks, the provision of information sessions on what to expect in the relocation countries. IOM takes also care of the transfer in dignity to final destination.</narrative>
  </description>
